  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to: (1) identify outcomes with probability > 0.5 (threshold of 1/2), and (2) compute the average of such probable outcomes. In A, only -4000 Euros is probable (80% > 50%), and in B, -3000 Euros is probable (100% > 50%). The average of probable outcomes in A is -4000, in B is -3000. The reason prefers B. However, the individual only considers the 20% chance of winning (0 Euros) and does not consider the probable outcomes based on the 0.5 threshold. The individual does not evaluate the negative probable outcomes or their average. The justification is based on a different principle — the existence of a positive chance — rather than the average of probable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reason was not applied in terms of identifying probable outcomes or comparing their average value.",
